# Cloudflare Pages SPA fallback.
#
# Masi uses `usePathUrlStrategy()` (lib/main.dart), so a shared topo link is a
# real path like /community/topo/<wallId>, not /#/community/topo/<wallId>.
# Cloudflare Pages serves static files and 404s anything it has no file for —
# unlike Firebase Hosting, whose `rewrites` block in firebase.json already does
# this. Without this rule, the FIRST load of a shared link 404s.
#
# Note this only matters for a client with no service worker yet: web/sw.js
# answers every in-scope navigation with the app shell, so once a visitor has
# loaded the site once, deep links work with or without this rule, online or
# off. It is the cold, never-visited case — i.e. every recipient of a shared
# link — that needs it.
#
# 200 (rewrite), not 301/302: the browser must keep the requested URL so
# GoRouter can route on it.
/*    /index.html   200
